From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 04:17:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: do not hold the first J604 panel
 frames after idle

swap_pace holds an internal-panel swap for the 120 Hz grid only while a
1/8 EWMA of the intervals between swap completions is at video rate. An
idle gap entered the average as 50 ms, so the average stayed above the
video threshold for the first six or so frames of any burst after idle,
and those frames were held for up to a tick: measured on the J604, the
first six frames of a terminal window opening after 0.76 s of idle and
the first three of the next burst were held, while the rest of the
120 Hz animation went as soon as possible.

Start the average afresh after an idle gap instead, so that the first
interval after it decides alone. A burst after idle (a keystroke, a
window opening, the first scroll step) is not held; a video resuming
after a pause is paced again from its second frame, since its first
interval is already at video rate.

Fixes: d18088e3ecbb ("drm/apple: m4: hold J604 panel frames for the grid only at video rates")
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 24597b8811..d2747db9cf 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -1148,7 +1148,7 @@ struct dcp_m4_runtime {
 	u64 pace_n[6];
 	u64 pace_over_sum;
 	u64 pace_over_max;
-	/* Smoothed interval between internal-panel swap completions (counter ticks, 1/8 EWMA) */
+	/* Smoothed interval between internal-panel swap completions (1/8 EWMA, 0 after idle) */
 	u64 int_prev_done;
 	u64 int_iv_ewma;
 	struct dcp_m4_properties *properties;
@@ -1782,10 +1782,20 @@ static void dcp_m4_pace_learn(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r)
 	u64 e = READ_ONCE(r->pace_e);
 
 	if (r->int_prev_done && done > r->int_prev_done) {
-		/* An idle gap counts as 50 ms: a burst after it shows within frames. */
-		u64 iv = min_t(u64, done - r->int_prev_done, div_u64(arch_timer_get_cntfrq(), 20));
+		/*
+		 * An idle gap (50 ms or more) starts the average afresh, so the
+		 * first interval after it decides alone whether video follows.
+		 * Counted as 50 ms, it took the first six or so frames of any
+		 * burst after idle (a keystroke, a window opening) for video, and
+		 * they were held for the grid.
+		 */
+		u64 iv = done - r->int_prev_done;
 
-		WRITE_ONCE(r->int_iv_ewma, r->int_iv_ewma ? (r->int_iv_ewma * 7 + iv) / 8 : iv);
+		if (iv >= div_u64(arch_timer_get_cntfrq(), 20))
+			WRITE_ONCE(r->int_iv_ewma, 0);
+		else
+			WRITE_ONCE(r->int_iv_ewma,
+				   r->int_iv_ewma ? (r->int_iv_ewma * 7 + iv) / 8 : iv);
 	}
 	r->int_prev_done = done;
 	if (e) {
